{
  "_comment": "Passive animals (ADR 0022). Distances and speeds in metres (Minecraft blocks are 1 m, so its values carry over), times in seconds, health in half-hearts. food = items that tempt (the mob follows a player holding one), breed adults and grow babies; drops = death drop list like mining.json (adults only, as in Minecraft); shear = what shears give (sheep), the wool grows back when it grazes. biomes = where herds spawn when the land first comes near a player; weight = Minecraft's spawn weight among the species of a biome; group = herd size. Wildlife (ADR 0027): lays = {item, every_s [min, max]} (chickens); slow_fall = flaps down without fall damage; legs = 2 or 4; rarity = chance a herd of this species really spawns once picked (bears are rare); predator = {prey: species it hunts, hunt_every_s: hunger interval, sight_m, chase_m: run speed, attack: half-hearts, attack_s: between bites, reach_m, eat_s: time at a kill, aggressive_chance: share that also hunt the player, player_sight_m}; predators do not panic when hurt, they turn on the attacker. A kill leaves a carcass, not drops. New in ADR 0058: habitat = where herds spawn and live: land (default, on grass or snow, or the 'ground' materials), shore (land next to water), water (in rivers and lakes: swims, flops and suffocates on land), cave (cave air below the surface; biomes are ignored); moves = walk (default), hop (rabbits, frogs: short hops), swim (fish), fly (bats: flutter, hang from ceilings), paddle (ducks: walk and float on water); skittish_m = flees a player who comes this close (wild animals); defends = a grazer that turns on whoever hurt it (boar: predator rules for the attacker only); predator.pack = it hunts with the others of its herd. legs = 0 (fish), 2, 4, 6 (crabs, drawn as three pairs) or 8 (spiders).",
